From khansen at stat.Berkeley.EDU  Sat Mar  8 03:09:51 2008
From: khansen at stat.Berkeley.EDU (Kasper Daniel Hansen)
Date: Fri, 7 Mar 2008 18:09:51 -0800
Subject: [BioC] Why is my matrix transposed?
In-Reply-To: <47D19ECD.3070409@med.umich.edu>
References: <A4D6B310-B14C-4277-84E8-5C445E4173F2@cc.usu.edu>
	<47D19ECD.3070409@med.umich.edu>
Message-ID: <8C2FCF45-34F2-45E9-8F83-168953FA62A8@stat.berkeley.edu>

This probably happened because the object returned from justRMA  
changed from a exprSet to an ExpressionSet and that these two classes  
have different coercion rules But for both class exprs(OBJECT) returns  
the same matrix - hence write.exprs is stable.

So to summarize, my guess is that it has to do with changes in the  
underlying representation.

Kasper

